conventions[8]{rule,detail}:
  fetch_in_pages_only,"Pages and route handlers fetch; components receive props. Only AbOverlay, PressReleaseItem and InfiniteArticleFeed fetch client-side"
  caching_at_call_site,"revalidate is set per fetch() call, never as a route segment export. 3600 everywhere except reading-mode.ts at 300"
  api_routes_are_proxies,"/api/press-release and /api/company-articles exist purely so client components can reach the same services the pages use"
  rails_via_primitives,"Any new sidebar card should use ui/Rail.tsx primitives so company and article rails stay dimensionally identical"
  self_omitting_cards,"RailRow returns nothing for null/undefined/empty, which is how cards disappear rather than render blank labels"
  taxonomy_source,"lib/sectors.ts is the master data; prefer lib/taxonomy.ts helpers over the older lib/sector-mapper.ts"
  sanitize_by_runtime,"lib/sanitize.ts for anything server-side (regex, no DOM); DOMPurify only inside Body.tsx in the browser"
  languages_single_source,"lib/languages.ts resolves every API/URL/subdomain spelling - do not hand-roll language strings"

docs[10]{file,what,status}:
  docs/api-integration-2026-09-08.md,"Change report for the 2026-09-08 API cutover: what the backend fixed, what was rewired for press releases/events/companies, the two incidental fixes (SSR sanitiser 500, 2.4MB events cache), full verification log and the outstanding backend asks","CURRENT - supersedes the status of api-defect-report-2026-09-07.md, 2 of whose 3 reported 500s are now fixed"
  README.md,"Setup instructions and architecture claims","STALE - roughly 12 claims are false. Do NOT trust it for setup. Claims route groups, Zod, isomorphic-dompurify, @tailwindcss/typography, wired next-intl, a .env.example, a working USE_MOCK path, NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL, a src/lib/services layout and subdomain rewrites - none of which exist"
  docs/api-defect-report-2026-09-07.md,"Backend hand-off raised for the three FromSql 500s","PARTLY OBSOLETE - the two Sectors failures (press-release/{id}, by-company/{id}) were fixed 2026-09-08. Only the Companies failure on /api/Events/{id} is still open. Kept as the record of what was raised"
  docs/api-schemas/README.md,"How the schema capture was produced, captured 2026-08-27","Accurate. Flags SEC-01 and INF-01 as the two headline warnings. Notes the capture scripts (probe.py, gen.py, gaps.py) were NOT committed, so the docs cannot be regenerated from this repo"
  docs/api-schemas/_gaps.csv,"28 catalogued API gaps with severity, workaround and evidence","THE most useful planning file in the repo. 2 critical, 8 high, 14 medium, 3 low. Workaround is None for EVT-07, TAX-01, CO-04 and INF-01"
  docs/api-schemas/_index.csv,"33-row endpoint inventory with observed status and consuming service","Accurate. All 12 legacy rows recorded 503 at capture time; only 2 legacy endpoints are actually consumed"
  docs/api-schemas/_field-dictionary.csv,"280 fields across all entities","PARTLY REFRESHED - Event and EventRelease rows re-exported 2026-09-08; every other entity still reflects the 2026-08-27 capture"
  docs/api-schemas/_taxonomy-rename.csv,"22-row old-to-new naming contract for the sector/industry rename","Mostly current. The Industrial naming row still says TBD but taxonomy-migration.md section 4 records it as decided"
  docs/taxonomy-migration.md,"The sector-greater-than-industry realignment plan and hand-off","PARTIALLY DONE. Steps 1, 2 and 4 done; step 3 outstanding BY CHOICE; step 5 remaining; step 6 pending backend. Its line 9 claim that nothing in the running app changed is now out of date - commit e875b51 did land behaviour changes"
  log.md,"795-line raw dev-chat transcript of the A/B design session","DELETE AFTER EXTRACTING. Contains plaintext employee credentials (see blockers). Its design decisions are already captured in the ab_testing section above, so nothing of value is lost"

gaps:
  source: docs/api-schemas/_gaps.csv
  captured: 2026-08-27
  tally: "2 critical, 8 high, 14 medium, 3 low - as captured. NOT re-counted."
  stale_warning: "The CSV itself has NOT been edited. Re-probing on 2026-09-08 found ART-01, ART-07 and EVT-03 fixed on the live API; those three rows are annotated FIXED in critical_and_high below but still count toward the tally above. Re-run the capture before trusting the numbers."
  no_workaround_exists[4]: INF-01,TAX-01,CO-04,EVT-07
  critical_and_high[10]{id,entity,issue,blocks,workaround}:
    SEC-01,Company,"GET /api/Companies/{id} returns username and password as plaintext strings","not a UI blocker - a credential disclosure that reaches the browser","frontend reads the endpoint and ignores both fields, but they stay in the payload"
    INF-01,All,"Entire legacy API returns 503 on every /acnnewswireapi/api/v1/* path","the company press-release archive (its only working source) and the article-detail fallback",NONE
    ART-07,Article,"FIXED 2026-09-08 - GET /api/Articles/by-company/{id} was 500 on a missing Sectors column","nothing now. It is the company archive's sole source and it paginates","none needed; company-articles.ts reads it directly"
    ART-01,Article,"FIXED 2026-09-08 - sectors on the detail endpoint now returns a real ARRAY (was a JSON-encoded string)","nothing","parseSectors in acn-adapter.ts:23 already accepted both shapes, so the change landed without a code edit"
    ART-02,Article,"Four list endpoints return four different shapes, including companyID vs companyId casing","every consumer needs its own mapper and casing bugs fail silently","acn-adapter.ts, news-list.ts and company-articles.ts each map separately"
    ART-03,Article,"language is missing from the homepage, by-industry and search list endpoints","language tags cannot render in most feeds","CompanyArticle.language left optional and undefined"
    TAX-01,Taxonomy,"API returns comma sector spellings like 'Construct, Engineering' while lib/sectors.ts uses space forms","exact-match sector filters return nothing AND those articles map to no category, so they vanish from homepage rows",NONE
    EVT-01,Event,"No subtitle or descriptive line - only description, which holds an opaque acronym","readers cannot tell what an event is","hand-entered subtitle in src/data/mock-events.ts"
    EVT-02,Event,"No opening time or timezone - dates are date-only at midnight with no offset","a countdown can only be honest to the day","mock-events.ts hardcodes +08:00 and event-date.ts parses the offset out"
    EVT-03,Event,"PARTLY FIXED 2026-09-08 - compId and companies[] are now populated, but on only 121 of 839 events (14%). Previously they were null/[] on every event","the other 718 events can never resolve releases - there is still no direct event-to-release relation, only organiser-company + year via /api/Events/company/{id}/year/{year}","services/events.ts:fetchEventReleases covers the 121; the rest render an empty release list"

blockers[16]{id,severity,what,where,owner,status}:
  API-EVENTS-500,HIGH,"New API /api/Events/{id} returns 500: 'The required column Companies was not present in the results of a FromSql operation'","backend acnnewswire-api",backend,"Same bug class as the Sectors 500 that was fixed on the Articles endpoints 2026-09-08 - point the backend at that fix. WORKED AROUND on the frontend: services/events.ts:fetchEvent reads the list endpoint and filters, so nothing is blocked today"
  LEGACY-API-503,MEDIUM,"The whole legacy host is down","https://www.acnnewswire.com/acnnewswireapi - gap INF-01",backend,"DOWNGRADED from CRITICAL 2026-09-08. It is no longer the company archive source - company-articles.ts was cut over to the new API. It is now enrichment ONLY: language, location, views, supplier and origin url. Its one visible cost is that articles canonicalise to /article/english/ regardless of language. The call is bounded by a 2s AbortSignal so a dead host cannot stall article rendering"
  CREDS-IN-LOGMD,CRITICAL,"log.md is committed to git and contains plaintext employee username/password pairs, the assembled AB_USERS value, and the admin credential","log.md, roughly lines 421-437 and 780",us,"UNDOCUMENTED ANYWHERE ELSE. Rotate the passwords and purge from git history - deleting the file alone will not clear history"
  SEC-01,CRITICAL,"Public /api/Companies/{id} returns plaintext username and password, which reach the browser","gap SEC-01",backend,"Strip from the DTO. Frontend already ignores the fields but they are still transmitted"
  DEV-HOST-IN-PROD,HIGH,"Seven hardcoded references to development.acnnewswire.com, so a production deploy calls the dev host. No prod switch exists and NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL is a no-op","src/services/*.ts",us,"Undocumented. Commit d64d677 says dev.acnnewswire.com but the code uses development.acnnewswire.com"
  SEARCH-INDEX-STALE,MEDIUM,"/search is served from a static snapshot, so it goes stale between rebuilds and cannot see anything published after the last run","src/data/prefetched-articles.json",us,"DOWNGRADED 2026-09-09 - the snapshot is now rebuildable with scripts/prefetch-articles.mjs and holds real ids. It was CRITICAL-in-effect before that: every one of its 292 ids 404'd. Re-run the script periodically, or replace with a live query once the API grows a keyword search parameter"
  TAXONOMY-STEP3,HIGH,"Homepage sector rows drop roughly 28 articles because lib/sector-mapper.ts was left un-migrated, so search and the homepage disagree on what belongs to a sector","docs/taxonomy-migration.md section 5 step 3",us,"KNOWN AND INTENTIONAL - held back because it is a visible change. The fix is two one-line delegations: getSectorCategory = sectorOf, getArticleCategories = sectorsOf"
  TAX-01,HIGH,"Comma vs space sector spellings make exact-match filters return nothing","gap TAX-01",both,"No workaround. Root cause is TAX-02, the unused GET /api/v1/Sector/GetSectors endpoint the frontend bypasses by hardcoding"
  EVT-03,HIGH,"No event-to-release relation on any endpoint","gap EVT-03",backend,"Hand-mapped in event-article-mappings.json, 1 of 13 events done"
  REACT-COMPILER-DANGLING,MEDIUM,"reactCompiler:true was DELETED from next.config.ts as a hotfix (not commented out), but babel-plugin-react-compiler is still a pinned devDep with nothing consuming it","package.json:26 and commit 1ab5299",us,"Undocumented - no comment in next.config.ts. Either re-enable and retest, or drop the dep. The clearest unresolved hotfix in the tree"
  EVENTIMAGES-NOT-WHITELISTED,MEDIUM,"EVENT_IMAGE_BASE targets www.acnnewswire.com/eventimages but only /images/company/** is in remotePatterns, so next/image would reject event art",next.config.ts,us,Undocumented
  EVENTS-TWO-DATASETS,MEDIUM,"The events section runs on two disjoint datasets simultaneously: hand-written mock events keyed by slug for detail pages, and live API events keyed by numeric id for the listing","src/data/mock-events.ts vs src/services/events.ts",us,"Undocumented. The individual field gaps are in _gaps.csv but the two-dataset split is not"
  README-STALE,MEDIUM,"About 12 false claims send new developers down dead ends",README.md,us,Undocumented
  LINT-BROKEN,MEDIUM,"npm run lint cannot run at all: 'Cannot find module ajv/lib/refs/json-schema-draft-04.json' from eslint/lib/shared/ajv.js. The overrides.ajv ^8.18.0 pin in package.json is the cause - ajv v8 removed that file and eslint still requires it","package.json:31 overrides.ajv",us,"Found 2026-09-08, undocumented anywhere else. So the repo has NEITHER a test runner NOR a working linter"
  NO-TEST-RUNNER,MEDIUM,"Neither file in src/lib/__tests__ can run - no test script and no runner installed. languages.test.ts is a real 31-assertion suite that needs tsx",package.json,us,"Known and noted in taxonomy-migration.md"
  GLOBALS-CSS-TYPO,LOW,"globals.css defines --text-csolor while body reads var(--text-color), so body colour silently falls back. The dark-mode block is also commented out",src/app/globals.css:7,us,Undocumented

current_steps[14]{priority,step,owner,why}:
  1,"Redeploy. The Sectors 500 is fixed and articles render again - the deployed portal is still serving the broken build",us,"Nothing ships until a fresh Netlify build runs. Verify an article URL on portal.acnnewswire.com afterwards, not just locally"
  2,"Get the backend to fix /api/Events/{id} - same 'required column' FromSql bug they just fixed on Articles",backend,"Frontend works around it by filtering the list endpoint, but that pulls 2.4MB to read one event"
  3,"Rotate the A/B employee passwords and purge log.md from git history",us,"Committed plaintext credentials"
  4,"Have the backend strip username and password from the Companies DTO",backend,"Credential disclosure on a public endpoint (SEC-01)"
  5,"Introduce an env-driven API base and stop shipping the dev host in production builds",us,"Deploy hygiene; also makes it possible to point at a healthy backend without a code change"
  6,"Finish taxonomy migration step 3 - two one-line delegations in sector-mapper.ts",us,"Makes the homepage and search agree and surfaces roughly 28 currently-hidden articles"
  7,"Decide the search story. NOTE: a live query is NOT currently possible - /api/Articles/search has no keyword parameter (only ExchangeId/SectorName/CompanyName/TickerId/Country) and returns [] for all of them. So either re-run scripts/prefetch-articles.js as a stopgap, or ask the backend for a keyword search endpoint",us,"The search index has been frozen since June and cannot return anything published since May"
  7b,"Get the legacy host back up or replace it",backend,"Downgraded from critical - it is now enrichment only. Without it every article canonicalises to /article/english/ regardless of the language it is written in"
  8,"Register the first real A/B experiment: add an EXPERIMENTS entry, author public/ab-variants/<id>.css, add data-ab-target to the target markup",us,"The voting infrastructure is finished and idle - this is the only thing standing between it and use"
  9,"Rewrite README.md",us,"Roughly 12 claims are false; it actively misleads anyone onboarding"
  10,"Decide reactCompiler - re-enable in next.config.ts and retest, or drop babel-plugin-react-compiler",us,"Dangling devDep from an undocumented hotfix"
  11,"Delete dead code: lib/azure.ts, lib/search-mock-data.ts, lib/region-mapping.ts, services/index.ts, services/mock-press-release.ts, __tests__/sector-mapper.test.ts, and the next-intl dependency",us,"Reduces the surface a newcomer has to read"
  12,"Add a test runner so src/lib/__tests__/languages.test.ts can run",us,"A real 31-assertion suite exists and is currently unrunnable"
  13,"Commit the schema-capture scripts (probe.py, gen.py, gaps.py) and the taxonomy verification script",us,"They live only in a session scratchpad, so docs/api-schemas cannot be regenerated today"

history:
  recent_arc: "Aug 15 page building (sidebars, company page, language tags) -> Aug 27 documenting the backend's shortcomings (33 schema CSVs, 28 catalogued gaps, taxonomy migration plan) -> Sep 4 building an internal A/B design-review tool. The Aug 27 pivot is the tell: feature work hit a wall on backend data, so the effort went into writing the backend hand-off instead."
  hotfix_cluster_2026_05_28[3]{item,verdict}:
    nextjs_downgrade,"Did NOT stick and does not conflict with today's ^16.2.6. f387c63 went 16.2.4->16.2.3, then 38eae4c went 16.2.3->16.2.6. It was also nearly a no-op since ^16.2.4 already resolved to 16.2.6 - the real fix was the route.ts edits, so the commit messages misattribute it"
    dompurify_swap,"RESOLVED permanently. isomorphic-dompurify is gone, plain dompurify@^3.4.7 is in. Only README.md:29 is still stale about it"
    react_compiler,"NOT resolved - worked around by deletion. See the REACT-COMPILER-DANGLING blocker"
  commit_map[6]{commit,date,scope}:
    ad42ca1,2026-09-04,"A/B vote infrastructure. 26 files, +2059. Also committed log.md"
    e875b51,2026-08-27,"Taxonomy steps 2-4. 6 files: filter-data, search, taxonomy, event-industries, MainNav/Industry"
    1a14037,2026-08-27,"44 files, +2322. The whole docs/api-schemas capture, taxonomy-migration.md, lib/taxonomy.ts, mock-events.ts, event detail page and 6 event components"
